menu "BMDS audio"

    config BMDS_AUDIO_PRIORITY
        int "Audio device task priority"
        default 20
        range 1 24
        help
            The task that fills each audio device's DMA buffers (devplan/audio.md §5). It must
            meet a deadline of two periods, so it runs above everything but the display's
            restart task.

    config BMDS_AUDIO_CLIENT_PRIORITY
        int "Real-time audio client priority"
        default 19
        range 1 24
        help
            A program's thread while it cycles a real-time audio fd (devplan/audio.md §20): under
            the device's task, above the rest. One that stays out of its cycle for 4 periods is
            put back to its own priority until it cycles again.

    # The I2S interrupt must run while the flash is written (/flash): with the cache off
    # it still clears finished buffers, so a gap plays silence, not stale audio
    # (devplan/audio.md §16).
    config BMDS_AUDIO_IRAM_SAFE
        bool
        default y
        select I2S_ISR_IRAM_SAFE

endmenu
